
- The reference output voltage (vref, measured at 25 degC with VDDA = 1.8 V) should be between 1.00 V and 1.20 V.
- The temperature coefficient of vref (tc, peak-to-peak over -45..125 degC divided by average and span) should be no larger than 1900 ppm/degC.
- The line sensitivity of vref (ls, over a VDDA sweep 1.62..1.98 V) should be no larger than 0.4 per volt.
- The power supply rejection ratio at low frequency (psrr, 10 Hz) should be at least 13 dB.
- The power supply rejection ratio at high frequency (psrr_hf, 1 MHz) should be at least 7 dB.
- The quiescent power consumption at 25 degC and VDDA = 1.8 V should be no larger than 22 uW.
